# Repositories the bot reviews, one line per repo:  owner/name  [filter]  [actions]
# Copy this to repos.conf and edit. '#' starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#
# Optional 2nd column = which PRs to review in that repo (overrides the global
# REVIEW_REQUESTED env default):
#   <login> / @me   only PRs that request this account as a reviewer (opt-in)
#   *               every open PR
#   (omitted)       fall back to the global REVIEW_REQUESTED default
#
# Optional 3rd column = what the verdict does (overrides the global REVIEW_ACTIONS
# default; requires a 2nd column to be present so the columns don't shift):
#   comment   post a COMMENT only — never approve/block (default, safest)
#   gate      verdict drives a review: green=APPROVE, red=BLOCKING REQUEST_CHANGES,
#             yellow=COMMENT (advises, does not block). A fork PR is never auto-approved. The bot still never
#             merges. NOTE: an APPROVE can satisfy branch-protection approval counts
#             — require a human/CODEOWNERS approval if a person must sign off.
#   (omitted) fall back to the global REVIEW_ACTIONS default (comment)
#
# In rotation mode (./auto-review.sh with no GH_REPO) each scheduled run reviews
# ONE repo from this list, advancing round-robin. With a 15-min timer that means
# repo #1 now, repo #2 in 15 min, repo #3 in 30 min, … — they are staggered, not
# all hit at once. Order here is the rotation order.
#
# ALL=1 ./auto-review.sh reviews every repo below in a single run (catch-up).

owner/first-repo        @me     # opt-in PRs, comment-only (default actions)
owner/second-repo       *       # every open PR, comment-only
owner/third-repo                # global REVIEW_REQUESTED + REVIEW_ACTIONS defaults
owner/gated-repo        @me  gate   # opt-in PRs; verdict APPROVES / REQUESTS-CHANGES
